WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.304
This practical lesson supports the school Week Five resuscitation outline. It integrates all eight saved sections of the AET manual-defibrillation supplement without repeating its patient story or completing a school assessment.
本实操准备课对应学校第5周复苏周纲，整合AET手动除颤补充课保存的全部八节，但不重复其患者故事，也不代做学校考核。

00:00:14.304 --> 00:00:29.112
The supplement is matched by topic, not explicitly allocated in the saved school directory. Its identical second entry is not another course. The explicitly assigned Seven C Part A remains the weekly module spine.
这门补充课是按主题对应，并非保存的学校目录明确分配；内容相同的第二入口也不是另一门课。本周主线仍是明确指定的7C Part A。

00:00:29.112 --> 00:00:42.720
Learn the decision and team sequence before memorizing a button. A school laboratory may teach a manual workflow, while a service-configured monitor can restrict which functions a particular operator may use.
先学决策和团队顺序，再记按钮。学校实验课可以教授手动流程，但机构配置的监护仪可能限制特定操作者可使用的功能。

00:00:42.720 --> 00:01:00.552
The linked bilingual reading identifies exact BCPEG pages and current-source differences. Device checkoffs, the actual school configuration and the restricted current PCP operating procedure remain unverified, so this is preparation, not credentialing.
下方中英对照阅读标明BCPEG具体页码及现行来源差异。实际器械考核、学校配置及受限的现行PCP操作规程仍未核实，所以这是学习准备，不是资质认证。

00:01:00.552 --> 00:01:13.440
Defibrillation delivers an electrical intervention to terminate certain dangerous ventricular rhythms. It does not pump blood for the patient, correct every cause or guarantee that a perfusing rhythm will follow.
除颤用电干预终止部分危险心室心律；它不会替患者泵血，不能纠正全部病因，也不能保证随后一定出现有灌注的心律。

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:27.528
The school three-phase model calls the early period electrical. It helps explain the urgency of treating VF or pulseless VT while myocardium is more viable, not a rule that every arrest starts in VF.
学校三阶段模型把早期称为电活动阶段，用来解释心肌尚较有活性时应尽快处理VF或无脉搏VT，而不是说每次骤停都从VF开始。

00:01:27.528 --> 00:01:39.192
If the defibrillator is available and a shock is indicated, do not delay that shock to finish a fixed period of CPR simply because the history suggests the patient is now in a later phase.
除颤器已可用且有电击指征时，不能因为病史似乎已进入较晚阶段，就为先做固定时长CPR而延迟电击。

00:01:39.192 --> 00:01:53.496
Continue good CPR during preparation and minimize the necessary assessment and shock pause. Early CPR and early defibrillation support each other; they are not competing treatments from which to choose only one.
准备期间继续高质量CPR，并尽量缩短必要的评估与电击停顿。早期CPR和早期除颤互相支持，不是只能二选一的竞争治疗。

00:01:53.496 --> 00:02:08.856
Arrest deprives cells of oxygen and metabolic substrate, reducing their ability to sustain electrical and mechanical function. Compressions generate limited circulation while definitive treatment and cause correction are organized.
骤停使细胞缺少氧和代谢底物，削弱其维持电活动与机械功能的能力。按压在组织决定性治疗及病因处理时，提供有限循环。

00:02:08.856 --> 00:02:21.648
Interruptions reduce perfusion pressure. Restarting compressions does not instantly restore everything lost during a pause. This explains the importance of planning equipment and exchanges before stopping.
停顿会降低灌注压力，而恢复按压不会立刻补回停顿所失。因此，要在停手前就计划好器械准备和换手。

00:02:21.648 --> 00:02:35.232
The school gives illustrative minute and pressure-recovery figures. They are not exact physiological clocks for every patient, and they do not establish an obligatory fifteen-second wait before assessing an indicated rhythm.
学校举出的分钟数和压力恢复时间用于说明概念，并不是每位患者精确的生理时钟，也不能规定每次有指征分析心律前都必须等十五秒。

00:02:35.232 --> 00:02:47.112
Measure actual hands-off intervals in practice. Improve an eight-second pause to a shorter safe pause rather than accepting eight seconds merely because it sits below a published upper bound.
练习时应测实际离手间隔。即使八秒低于某来源的上限，也应争取缩短为更短且安全的停顿，而不是因此直接接受八秒。

00:02:47.112 --> 00:03:01.224
The later metabolic phase describes worsening cellular injury and complex injury after circulation returns. It is useful physiology, but a ten-minute boundary does not prove irreversible death in an individual.
较晚的代谢阶段描述细胞损伤加重，以及循环恢复后的复杂损伤。这是有用的生理模型，但十分钟界线不能证明某个人已经不可逆死亡。

00:03:01.224 --> 00:03:14.040
Arrest duration is only one part of the history. Distinguish time without any circulation-supporting CPR from time with effective CPR, and recognize special causes such as hypothermia.
骤停时长只是病史的一部分。要区分完全没有支持循环的CPR时间，与有效CPR期间，并识别低温等特殊病因。

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:25.896
Do not teach the school survival-per-minute percentage as a personalized prognosis, or a progression from coarse VF to fine VF to asystole as a mandatory sequence in every case.
不能把学校每分钟生存下降百分比当作个人预后，也不能说每次都必然按粗VF、细VF、心静止的顺序发展。

00:03:25.896 --> 00:03:40.320
Withholding, discontinuation and recognition of life extinct follow their actual pathways. The preceding Seven C lecture teaches those distinctions; a phase label or monitor appearance does not replace them.
不开始复苏、终止复苏和确认生命消逝各有实际流程。前一7C课已讲这些区别，阶段名称或监护外观都不能替代它们。

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:54.792
The chain of survival includes recognition, response activation, CPR, defibrillation when indicated, advanced care and post-arrest recovery. Completing a later link does not make an earlier link unnecessary.
生存链包括识别、启动响应、CPR、有指征除颤、高级照护及骤停后恢复。完成后面的环节，并不会让前面的环节变得不必要。

00:03:54.792 --> 00:04:08.040
For example, an access operator can prepare a line while the compressor works and the defibrillator operator prepares pads. Access must not become the reason the first useful shock is delayed.
例如，建立通路者可与按压者及准备电极的除颤操作者并行工作。不能因为建立通路而延迟第一次有效电击机会。

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:22.104
Use additional personnel where they improve a specific task. If there are fewer people, combine roles deliberately and prioritize lifesaving actions rather than trying to perform every textbook task simultaneously.
新增人员应分配到能实际改善的任务上。人少时应有意识地兼任并排序，不能试图同时完成教材中每一项操作。

00:04:22.104 --> 00:04:33.408
A useful leader continually asks what is preventing effective oxygen delivery now. That question connects technique to the patient instead of turning the arrest into a checklist race.
有效的带领者不断问：现在是什么妨碍有效氧输送？这样才能把技术连回患者，而不是把骤停处理变成清单竞速。

00:04:33.408 --> 00:04:48.984
Allocate compression, airway, defibrillator, leadership and recording functions. Add medication or access roles according to people and authority. A role title alone does not confirm that its essential tasks are being done.
分配按压、气道、除颤、带领及记录职能；根据人手和权限增加给药或通路角色。只有角色名称，并不能确认关键任务实际有人完成。

00:04:48.984 --> 00:05:01.968
Say a name and a concrete action, receive a read-back, then expect completion or a barrier report. If a device is not ready, that fact must reach the leader before a planned pause begins.
应叫名字并说清具体动作，获得复述后，再接收完成或障碍报告。器械尚未准备好时，必须在计划停顿前让带领者知道。

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:13.512
The compressor should announce fatigue and the next operator should be ready before the exchange. The recorder can warn of the approaching cycle boundary without dictating an unsafe interruption.
按压者应通报疲劳，接替者应在换手前准备好。记录者可以提醒循环即将结束，但不能因此指挥一次不安全停顿。

00:05:13.512 --> 00:05:25.632
When new responders arrive, give a short patient-state and treatment summary before assigning a gap. An unbriefed extra person at the chest can create confusion rather than useful capacity.
新响应者到场时，先简短介绍患者状态和治疗经过，再安排缺口任务。未经简报就多站一人在胸前，可能增加混乱而非有效能力。

00:05:25.632 --> 00:05:40.104
For this adult practical, combine a rate of one hundred to one hundred twenty with appropriate five to six centimeter depth, full recoil and minimal interruptions. A metronome checks timing, not all of these dimensions.
本成人实操应结合每分钟100至120次、适当的5至6厘米深度、充分回弹及最少停顿。节拍器检查的是时序，而不是全部质量维度。

00:05:40.104 --> 00:05:54.240
Keep shoulders and hands appropriately aligned and avoid leaning between compressions. Full recoil means releasing downward pressure, not repeatedly removing all contact and losing the correct location.
让肩、手保持适当对齐，按压间避免倚靠。充分回弹是释放向下压力，并不是每次都完全抬离而丢掉正确位置。

00:05:54.240 --> 00:06:06.912
Use a suitable firm support and the actual training feedback. Rotate about every two minutes, or sooner if quality declines, coordinating the transition with a necessary pause whenever feasible.
使用合适坚实支撑及实际训练反馈。约每两分钟更换，质量下降时更早换，并尽可能把交接与必要停顿协调在一起。

00:06:06.912 --> 00:06:17.592
An impressive compression fraction can still coexist with shallow or poorly positioned compressions. Review the whole performance rather than celebrating one favorable number.
很高的按压时间比例，仍可能伴浅按压或位置不佳。应审查整体表现，而不是只庆祝一个好看的数字。

00:06:17.592 --> 00:06:33.144
In the current local adult pathway, use thirty compressions and two breaths without an advanced airway. With an appropriate advanced airway, continuous compressions and roughly one breath each six seconds are the relevant adult framework.
现行当地成人流程中，没有高级气道时采用30次按压配2次送气；适当高级气道建立后，采用连续按压及约每六秒一次送气的成人框架。

00:06:33.144 --> 00:06:46.200
Coordinate ventilation with the compressor and avoid unnecessarily long pauses. Deliver enough to produce appropriate chest rise, not an aggressive squeeze intended to inflate the lungs as much as possible.
通气要与按压者配合，避免不必要长停顿。送气应达到适当胸廓起伏，而不是为了把肺尽量充满而猛烈挤压。

00:06:46.200 --> 00:07:00.912
Excessive rate or volume raises intrathoracic pressure and can impair venous return. Hypocapnia after ROSC can also reduce cerebral blood flow; faster breathing is not automatically better oxygen delivery.
过快或过大通气会提高胸内压，可能妨碍静脉回流；ROSC后的低二氧化碳还可能减少脑血流。因此，呼吸越快并不等于氧输送越好。

00:07:00.912 --> 00:07:17.184
If the waveform changes or chest rise is poor, evaluate airway position, obstruction, seal and the device while the team maintains the necessary arrest care. Do not solve an unexplained low CO2 by blindly increasing ventilation.
波形改变或胸廓起伏不佳时，应检查气道位置、梗阻、密合及器械，同时维持必要骤停照护。不能面对原因不明的低CO2，就盲目加快通气。

00:07:17.184 --> 00:07:30.456
An AED analyzes a signal through its specified electrodes and advises or delivers treatment according to its design. A semiautomatic AED still requires an operator to press the shock control when prompted.
AED通过规定电极分析信号，并依设计建议或实施治疗。半自动AED在提示后，仍需要操作者按下电击控制。

00:07:30.456 --> 00:07:44.880
Manual operation moves rhythm interpretation and energy selection to a trained, authorized person. Skilled use may shorten pauses, but a confident misinterpretation can also produce an inappropriate shock.
手动操作把心律判断和能量选择交给受训且有权限的人。熟练操作可能缩短停顿，但自信的误判同样可能造成不恰当电击。

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:57.504
Biphasic describes reversal of current direction during the waveform. It does not make every manufacturer use the same joules or mean that a device automatically delivers only the energy the patient needs.
双相指电流在波形中改变方向，并不表示所有厂家使用相同焦耳，也不表示器械会自动只给患者需要的能量。

00:07:57.504 --> 00:08:09.552
Do not delay an available, appropriate AED shock just to replace it with a preferred manual device. Coordinate any transition so that working CPR and defibrillation are not lost.
不能只为换成更喜欢的手动器械，而延迟已经可实施的适当AED电击。任何转换都应协调，不能丢掉正在有效进行的CPR和除颤。

00:08:09.552 --> 00:08:21.576
Confirm whether the device is in manual therapy, AED prompted protocol or advisory monitoring. Similar-looking screens can support different functions and different operator permissions.
先确认器械处于手动治疗、AED提示流程还是建议监护。外观相似的屏幕可能支持不同功能，也对应不同操作者权限。

00:08:21.576 --> 00:08:35.280
The official LIFEPAK manual describes settings that can restrict manual access, require confirmation or require a passcode. This is a device capability description, not a reason to circumvent restrictions.
官方LIFEPAK说明书描述了可限制手动访问、要求确认或要求口令的设置。这是在说明器械能力，不是绕过限制的理由。

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:47.016
The current linked BCEHS PCP operating procedure is login restricted and has not been read. We do not infer its present settings from an old factory default or from a school supplement.
当前链接的BCEHS PCP操作规程需要登录，尚未读到。不能从较旧的出厂默认值或学校补充课推断其中现行设置。

00:08:47.016 --> 00:09:00.288
Synchronized cardioversion and pacing are advanced interventions in this context. Knowing what SYNC or PACER means helps avoid errors; it does not authorize a learner to initiate those therapies.
在这里，同步心律转复及起搏属于高级干预。理解SYNC和PACER的意义有助于防错，但不会授权学员启动这些治疗。

00:09:00.288 --> 00:09:12.216
Check device readiness, power and compatible in-date pads and cable. The ECG cable used to monitor a rhythm is not automatically the therapy connection used to deliver a shock.
核对器械可用、电源、相容且未过期的电极和线缆。用于监护心律的ECG线，并不自动等同于实施电击的治疗连接。

00:09:12.216 --> 00:09:26.712
Expose and prepare enough chest for correct pad placement while preserving dignity where possible. Remove obstructing clothing and moisture and address excessive hair without turning preparation into a prolonged pause.
在尽可能维护尊严的同时，暴露并准备足够胸部以正确贴电极。移除遮挡衣物和水分，处理过多胸毛，但不能把准备拖成长期停顿。

00:09:26.712 --> 00:09:40.032
Use the device instructions for skin preparation, approved accessories and connections. Do not put extra paddle gel under adhesive pads or improvise an incompatible connector to save a few seconds.
皮肤准备、附件和连接应按器械说明。不能在自粘电极下再加电极板导电胶，也不能为省几秒而临时改接不相容接头。

00:09:40.032 --> 00:09:52.320
Announce readiness before the team commits to an assessment pause. If the cable remains disconnected, continue useful CPR while that problem is fixed instead of making everyone wait with hands off.
团队准备进入评估停顿前，应先通报已就绪。线缆仍未连接时，应在解决问题的同时继续有效CPR，不能让所有人离手等着。

00:09:52.320 --> 00:10:05.208
For the adult anterior-lateral arrangement, place one electrode on the upper right chest below the clavicle and the other on the left lateral chest with the pad center near the midaxillary line as appropriate.
成人前外侧位置，一片在右上胸锁骨下，另一片在左侧胸，使电极中心在适当的腋中线附近。

00:10:05.208 --> 00:10:20.328
Adapt to actual anatomy, avoid obstructing patches or implanted-device sites when possible, and obtain full skin contact. A pad balanced on a fold or only partly attached may not transmit energy effectively.
根据实际解剖调整，尽可能避开遮挡的贴剂或植入装置部位，并确保完整皮肤接触。贴在褶皱上或只粘住一部分，可能无法有效传递能量。

00:10:20.328 --> 00:10:35.304
The reviewed LP15 instructions distinguish an anterior-posterior option for manual therapy from its anterior-lateral requirement in AED mode. Do not turn an alternative placement from one mode into a universal rule for another.
已核对的LP15说明书区分了手动治疗可用的前后位，与其AED模式要求的前外侧位。不能把一个模式的替代位置变成另一个模式的通用规则。

00:10:35.304 --> 00:10:49.104
Inspect adhesion before discharge and after movement. If an electrode must be moved, follow its replacement instructions rather than assuming a lifted, dried pad can always be stuck back with equal performance.
放电前及移动后都要检查粘附。如果需要移动电极，应依更换说明处理，不能假定揭起、变干后再粘回仍有同样性能。

00:10:49.104 --> 00:11:01.776
The school supplement uses two hundred joules as its initial adult LIFEPAK example. Learn that labelled school example, but do not export it as the one initial dose for every biphasic defibrillator.
学校补充课用200 J作为成人LIFEPAK初始能量示例。应记清这是学校示例，不能把它推广成所有双相除颤器唯一的初始剂量。

00:11:01.776 --> 00:11:18.096
For real use, the authorized operator follows the applicable protocol and exact model configuration, including any escalation. A numbered setting, a charged energy display and an actual delivered-shock record are different observations.
实际使用中，有权限的操作者应遵循适用流程及具体机型配置，包括能量递增。选定数字、已充能显示和实际电击记录，是不同观察。

00:11:18.096 --> 00:11:32.616
Confirm the intended setting before charging and confirm available energy before discharge. A mechanical patient twitch is not reliable proof of delivered energy, and absence of ROSC is not proof of equipment failure.
充能前确认目标设置，放电前确认可用能量。患者机械性抽动不能可靠证明能量已送出，没有ROSC也不能证明器械故障。

00:11:32.616 --> 00:11:46.776
Do not use a universal energy range from a general nursing table, or assume smaller pads automatically reduce manual energy. Those shortcuts can turn an otherwise coordinated workflow into an incorrect treatment.
不能使用普通护理表中的通用能量范围，也不能以为小电极会自动降低手动能量。这些捷径会把原本配合良好的流程变成错误治疗。

00:11:46.776 --> 00:12:00.792
The school COACHED sequence keeps compressions going while the operator prepares. It calls out oxygen management, others clear, charging, hands off, rhythm evaluation and either defibrillation or disarming.
学校COACHED顺序让操作者准备时按压继续，并依次叫出氧气处理、其他人员离开、充能、离手、心律评估，以及电击或撤能。

00:12:00.792 --> 00:12:14.640
Translate each word into an observed action. Oxygen away requires the airway person to manage the actual oxygen source, not somebody merely repeating the phrase while free-flow oxygen remains at the chest.
每个词都必须对应可见动作。氧气移开意味着气道人员实际处理氧源，而不是自由流动氧仍在胸前，旁人只把口令念一遍。

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:31.440
The supplement gives a one-meter free-flow oxygen example; the reviewed manufacturer warning requires managing nearby oxygen sources. Follow the actual equipment fire-safety procedure rather than indiscriminately disconnecting every secured ventilation circuit.
补充课举自由流动氧移开一米的例子；已核对的厂家警告要求处理附近氧源。应按实际器械防火流程，不能不分情况地断开所有已固定的通气回路。

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:43.704
The person still compressing must explicitly acknowledge clearing before discharge. This is why a memorized rapid chant cannot replace a visual check of people, patient and equipment.
仍在按压的人，必须在放电前明确回应已离开。这就是为什么背得很快的口令不能替代对人员、患者和器械的目视检查。

00:12:43.704 --> 00:12:56.328
In the taught manual workflow, charging can occur while compressions continue. Nobody should interpret a charge tone as an instruction to deliver an immediate shock with the compressor still touching the patient.
在所教手动流程中，充能时可以继续按压，但不能把充能声当成按压者仍接触患者时立即放电的指令。

00:12:56.328 --> 00:13:11.712
Before discharge, ensure no person is touching the patient, stretcher, bed or conductive equipment in contact with the patient. Look for an unnoticed hand, a helper holding a limb or a rescuer leaning on a rail.
放电前确认无人接触患者、担架、床或与患者接触的导电设备。应寻找未注意到的手、扶着肢体的协助者，或倚在栏杆上的救援者。

00:13:11.712 --> 00:13:23.856
Adhesive pads are not hand-held paddles. Do not press on adhesive therapy pads during discharge or copy a paddle-pressure instruction onto a hands-free electrode workflow.
自粘电极不是手持电极板。放电时不能按住自粘治疗电极，也不能把电极板的加压指令套入免手持电极流程。

00:13:23.856 --> 00:13:36.000
A last-second safety concern overrides the desire for a fast pause. Stop the unsafe action, make the situation safe and minimize the additional interruption without skipping the check.
最后一刻出现的安全问题，优先于追求停顿速度。应阻止不安全动作、排除风险，并缩短额外停顿，而不是跳过检查。

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:49.296
A rhythm assessment requires an interpretable ECG. Compression and movement artifact can resemble ventricular activity; a dramatic screen during active compressions is not enough to select a shock.
心律评估需要可解释ECG。按压和移动伪差可能像心室活动；持续按压时屏幕看起来很乱，并不足以决定电击。

00:13:49.296 --> 00:14:05.520
At the coordinated brief assessment, identify VF, pulseless VT, asystole or an organized pattern in the patient context. Pulselessness is a clinical state, not an automatic label attached to every wide complex.
在协调好的短暂评估中，应结合患者识别VF、无脉搏VT、心静止或规则电活动。无脉搏是临床状态，不能自动贴给所有宽QRS。

00:14:05.520 --> 00:14:17.640
State the decision clearly so the compressor and recorder know what follows. An organized rhythm alone does not justify repeated prolonged pulse checks outside the appropriate assessment sequence.
把决定清楚说出，让按压者和记录者知道下一步。单有规则心律，不足以让团队在适当评估顺序之外反复长时间查脉搏。

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:31.536
Aim for the shortest safe assessment and shock pause. If equipment uncertainty cannot be resolved immediately, maintain necessary CPR and address the specific uncertainty rather than prolonging hands-off debate.
目标是最短且安全的评估与电击停顿。器械疑点不能立即解决时，应维持必要CPR并处理具体疑点，而不是离手长时间争论。

00:14:31.536 --> 00:14:43.368
When the rhythm is shockable and safety and energy are verified, the operator delivers the shock using the correct control. Announce delivery so everyone understands the transition.
心律可电击，并确认安全与能量后，由操作者使用正确控制实施电击，再通报电击已完成，让所有人理解流程转换。

00:14:43.368 --> 00:14:55.008
Immediately restart compressions after the shock in the ongoing arrest pathway. Do not spend the next interval staring at the screen or routinely checking for a pulse just to see whether the shock worked.
持续骤停流程中，电击后立即重新按压。不能把接下来时间用来盯屏，也不能只为看电击是否有效就常规立即查脉搏。

00:14:55.008 --> 00:15:05.688
Continue ventilation, planned exchanges and investigation of causes without allowing the delivered shock to become an unstructured pause in all other treatment.
继续通气、计划换手和病因检查，不能让一次电击变成其他治疗全部失去组织的停顿。

00:15:05.688 --> 00:15:20.616
Record the actual delivered energy and time, not just what was selected. If spontaneous signs suggest a real state change, communicate and assess appropriately rather than ignoring the patient to finish a fixed cycle blindly.
记录实际送出的能量和时间，而不只是选择值。如果自主迹象提示真正状态改变，应通报并适当评估，不能为盲目做完固定循环而忽视患者。

00:15:20.616 --> 00:15:32.832
A precharged device does not commit the team to a shock. If assessment does not support defibrillation, announce that decision and remove the unwanted charge through the device disarm procedure.
预先充能并不意味着团队必须电击。评估不支持除颤时，应通报决定，并通过器械撤能流程清除不需要的能量。

00:15:32.832 --> 00:15:46.608
The reviewed LIFEPAK manual describes pressing the speed dial to cancel a charge. It also describes automatic disarming under certain conditions, but waiting for a timeout is not the same as deliberately securing the device.
已核对的LIFEPAK说明书描述按Speed Dial取消充能，也描述某些情况下自动撤能。但等超时，不等于主动确保器械安全。

00:15:46.608 --> 00:15:58.752
Do not discharge into the air or give an unnecessary patient shock merely to empty the capacitor. Verify the actual disarmed state rather than assuming the phrase charge dumped completed the action.
不能对空气放电，也不能只为清空电容给患者不必要电击。应确认真实撤能状态，而不是以为说了撤能完成，就已经做到了。

00:15:58.752 --> 00:16:09.648
Resume necessary CPR promptly after the assessment. The operator can confirm device status while the team returns to nonshockable care and cause-directed thinking.
评估后应迅速恢复必要CPR。团队回到不可电击照护及病因思考时，操作者继续确认器械状态。

00:16:09.648 --> 00:16:23.448
True asystole and PEA are nonshockable arrest states. Continue effective CPR, ventilation and appropriate cause management; increasing joules does not turn them into indications for defibrillation.
真正心静止及PEA属于不可电击骤停状态。应继续有效CPR、通气和适当病因处理；提高焦耳不会让它们变成除颤指征。

00:16:23.448 --> 00:16:35.472
An AED no-shock message does not establish a pulse, prove good signal quality or certify death. Combine the message with the patient assessment and troubleshoot contradictory findings.
AED提示不建议电击，并不证明有脉搏、信号良好或已经死亡。应结合患者评估，并对矛盾发现进行排查。

00:16:35.472 --> 00:16:49.248
PEA can appear narrow or wide, fast or slow. The important immediate distinction is organized electrical activity without effective circulation, not memorizing one single strip appearance.
PEA可窄可宽、可快可慢。即时关键是有规则电活动却无有效循环，而不是记住唯一一种心电条外观。

00:16:49.248 --> 00:17:00.408
Continue the applicable reassessment cycle and early consultation planning. A single nonshockable assessment is not a new timer-based permission to terminate resuscitation.
继续适用复评循环，并规划早期咨询。一次不可电击评估，并不会产生新的按计时终止复苏权限。

00:17:00.408 --> 00:17:14.760
For an unexpected trace, check the patient and the signal chain: skin contact, compatible cable, electrode connection, displayed source and motion. Do not assume every irregular waveform is VF.
遇到意外波形，应检查患者及信号链：皮肤接触、相容线缆、电极连接、显示来源和移动。不能把所有不规则波形都当VF。

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:29.424
The LP15 AED warning requires stopping a moving vehicle for analysis and standing clear. Manual interpretation is also affected by artifact; changing the mode does not magically create a reliable ECG.
LP15的AED警告要求分析时停车并离开接触。手动判断同样受伪差影响，换模式不会神奇地生成可靠ECG。

00:17:29.424 --> 00:17:43.560
If pads do not adhere, correct the cause and replace unsuitable pads according to the instructions. If the monitor loses power, assign troubleshooting or a backup while the rest of the team sustains essential care.
电极粘不牢时，应纠正原因并按说明更换不合适电极。监护仪掉电时，分配人员排查或准备备用器械，其余团队继续关键照护。

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:56.568
Avoid a long global stop while several people inspect the same connector. Say the precise fault and assign one owner, with a clear plan for rhythm assessment and defibrillation as soon as feasible.
不能让多人围着同一接头查看而全局长时间停止。应说清具体故障，指定一人负责，并明确尽早恢复心律分析和除颤的计划。

00:17:56.568 --> 00:18:09.360
A flat-looking screen may represent asystole, a disconnected source, an unsuitable display setting or low-amplitude activity. Do not diagnose death from the first glance at one trace.
看似平直的屏幕，可能是心静止、信号断开、显示设置不合适或低幅活动。不能只看一条波形第一眼就判断死亡。

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:23.520
Inspect connection and source, and use appropriate leads or display assessment according to the device and local procedure. The goal is a reliable interpretation, not adjusting the screen until it resembles a shockable rhythm.
应按器械与当地流程检查连接和来源，并使用适当导联或显示评估。目标是获得可靠判断，不是把屏幕调到像可电击心律为止。

00:18:23.520 --> 00:18:35.808
Do not reflexively shock an uncertain flat line. Keep the assessment focused and brief, return to useful CPR and obtain the needed expertise without unnecessary delay.
不能对不确定的平直线反射性电击。评估应集中、短暂，恢复有效CPR，并及时取得所需专长。

00:18:35.808 --> 00:18:47.280
Document what was actually visible and what checks were made. Do not write confirmed asystole simply because the initial electrode was disconnected or the display was unreadable.
应记录实际可见内容及做过的检查，不能只因为最初电极断开或屏幕无法读，就写已经确认心静止。

00:18:47.280 --> 00:18:59.376
Defibrillation, synchronized cardioversion and transcutaneous pacing are not interchangeable settings for a sick patient. They address different electrical and clinical problems.
除颤、同步心律转复和经皮起搏，不是病情严重时可随意互换的设置，它们处理不同电活动及临床问题。

00:18:59.376 --> 00:19:12.456
A wide fast rhythm with a definite pulse is not automatically pulseless VT. Assess hemodynamic instability and request the appropriate advanced help rather than choosing the arrest shock pathway from width alone.
明确有脉搏的宽快心律，并不自动是无脉搏VT。应评估血流动力学不稳定并请求适当高级帮助，不能只凭宽QRS就选骤停电击流程。

00:19:12.456 --> 00:19:24.384
A very slow perfusing rhythm may need urgent advanced treatment. It is not corrected by defibrillating a nonshockable rhythm or improvising an unsupervised pacing setup.
很慢但仍有灌注的心律可能需要紧急高级治疗，但不能靠给不可电击心律除颤，或自行安排无人监督的起搏来解决。

00:19:24.384 --> 00:19:38.400
In this PCP learner context, recognition, supportive care, early escalation and preparation are the task. Device capability and an educational explanation do not expand procedural authority.
在这里的PCP学员情境中，任务是识别、支持照护、尽早升级和准备。器械功能与教学解释都不会扩大操作权限。

00:19:38.400 --> 00:19:52.488
The school supplement repeatedly generalizes that AEDs are not intended for children under eight. The reviewed LP15 AED mode does have that restriction; AEDs in general do not share a universal under-eight ban.
学校补充课反复笼统说AED不适合八岁以下。已核对的LP15 AED模式确实有这一限制，但不能说所有AED都统一禁用于八岁以下。

00:19:52.488 --> 00:20:06.264
Current AHA and AAP guidance supports pediatric attenuation when available, trained manual defibrillation where appropriate, and consideration of a nonattenuated AED if the preferred options are unavailable.
现行AHA和AAP指导支持有条件时使用儿童能量衰减、在适当情况下由受训者手动除颤；优先选项都没有时，可考虑无衰减AED。

00:20:06.264 --> 00:20:19.920
Pads must fit without overlap and be compatible with the actual equipment. On the reviewed LP15, attaching pediatric electrodes does not automatically select a weight-based energy dose.
电极必须相容、能贴合且不重叠。已核对的LP15连接儿童电极后，并不会自动选择按体重计算的能量。

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:33.960
This comparison prevents an unsafe generalization; it is not the complete pediatric course. Keep age-specific assessment, ventilation, energy and device training together rather than exporting adult defaults.
这项比较是为避免危险概括，并不是完整儿童课。年龄对应的评估、通气、能量和器械训练应放在一起，不能直接沿用成人默认值。

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:47.472
The supplement describes broad IO use in arrest and shock. Current local PR12 is more specific for independent PCP IO and distinguishes direct on-scene advanced supervision from a telephone consultation.
补充课广泛讨论骤停和休克使用IO，但现行当地PR12对PCP独立IO规定更具体，并区分高级人员现场直接监督与电话咨询。

00:20:47.472 --> 00:21:01.440
The previously taught independent branch is not every medical arrest: it includes the specified hypovolemic-arrest context, critical fluid need and unavailable or failed IV, with the other current limits.
前面教过的独立分支并不是所有内科骤停，而是包括规定的低血容量骤停背景、关键补液需要，以及IV不可用或失败，并满足其他现行限制。

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:15.576
PCP tibial site limits, age restrictions and collective attempt limits are not erased by a school humeral or pediatric example. Access does not automatically grant epinephrine or another advanced drug authority.
学校肱骨或儿童示例，不会取消PCP胫骨部位、年龄及共同尝试次数限制。建立了通路，也不会自动取得肾上腺素等高级药物权限。

00:21:15.576 --> 00:21:27.624
Use the Week Three vascular practical for the checked technical sequence. Here the operational question is who can perform which access task without delaying compressions or the indicated shock.
已核对的技术顺序见第3周血管通路实操。本课关注的是，谁可做哪项通路任务，并且不延迟按压或有指征电击。

00:21:27.624 --> 00:21:43.128
The supplement access sequence contains conflicting statements about flushing before versus after pain management. In an awake patient, use the actual analgesia and confirmation procedure rather than copying the first numbered list.
补充课的通路顺序，对先冲洗还是先处理疼痛存在矛盾。清醒患者应按实际镇痛与确认流程，不能直接抄第一份编号清单。

00:21:43.128 --> 00:21:57.552
Swelling, leakage or concerning resistance requires immediate attention. Do not pressurize a questionable line harder to achieve a nominal flow, and do not treat absent aspiration alone as automatic proof of failure.
肿胀、渗漏或令人担忧的阻力需要立即处理。不能为达到名义流量而对可疑通路加更大压力，也不能只因未抽到骨髓就自动断定失败。

00:21:57.552 --> 00:22:11.256
Secure and repeatedly inspect any functioning access, especially after movement. Distinguish device assistance from certainty: a pressure infuser cannot confirm that the tip is correctly positioned.
任何可用通路都应固定并反复检查，移动后尤其如此。器械辅助不等于确认正确，压力输液装置无法证明针尖位置正确。

00:22:11.256 --> 00:22:25.128
Communicate failure or an uncertain delivered dose accurately. Document the site, attempt, findings, action and response; do not invent a successful infusion because a bag volume decreased.
应准确通报失败或实际给入剂量不确定，记录部位、尝试、发现、行动和反应。不能只因输液袋体积减少，就编成已成功输入。

00:22:25.128 --> 00:22:39.984
A sudden sustained ETCO2 rise can suggest ROSC, but no universal thirty-five or forty millimeter threshold proves it. Ventilation, drugs, compression quality and sampling can also change the number.
ETCO2突然持续升高可以提示ROSC，但不存在一到35或40 mmHg就能证明的统一阈值。通气、药物、按压质量和采样也能改变数字。

00:22:39.984 --> 00:22:55.320
Communicate the clue and assess circulation appropriately. Once ROSC is confirmed, announce the transition so compressions, ventilation, monitoring and recording are intentionally coordinated rather than independently changed.
先通报线索并适当确认循环。确认ROSC后，应宣布转换，让按压、通气、监护和记录有意识地配合，而不是各自改变。

00:22:55.320 --> 00:23:12.240
Titrate oxygen with reliable measurement, avoid excessive ventilation, assess blood pressure and perfusion, maintain airway support and prepare for recurrence. The preceding lesson labels the actual N03 and other-source target differences.
依可靠测量滴定氧疗，避免过度通气，评估血压和灌注，维持气道支持并准备再骤停。前课已标示N03与其他来源的具体目标差异。

00:23:12.240 --> 00:23:27.888
Temperature management, cause-directed destination and early ECG communication remain important. Do not import a hospital temperature protocol, routine cold fluid or a prognostic judgment from one early neurological examination.
温度管理、针对病因的目的地选择和早期ECG沟通仍重要。不能直接搬用医院温控、常规冷液体，或凭一次早期神经检查判断预后。

00:23:27.888 --> 00:23:40.368
The LP15 advisory configuration allows monitoring functions while a background system looks for potentially shockable rhythms. It is not simply full manual therapy with a safety net switched on.
LP15建议监护配置允许使用监护功能，同时由后台系统寻找可能可电击的心律。它并不只是把完全手动治疗加上一个安全网。

00:23:40.368 --> 00:23:55.272
The reviewed manual says surveillance does not prompt for nonshockable rhythms such as asystole. A perfusing organized rhythm and PEA can also look electrically similar, so absence of an alert cannot establish safety.
已核对说明书指出，对心静止等不可电击心律，该监视系统不会发出相同提示。有灌注规则心律与PEA的电活动也可能相似，所以没有报警不能证明安全。

00:23:55.272 --> 00:24:10.536
A check-patient alert requires checking the patient. Motion, low signal amplitude and other problems can cause false alerts; do not press ANALYZE or shock a conscious perfusing person just because the device requested attention.
检查患者提示，要求先检查患者。移动、信号幅度低及其他问题可能误报；不能只因器械要求关注，就对清醒有灌注者按ANALYZE或电击。

00:24:10.536 --> 00:24:26.184
In the reviewed configured workflow, LEAD returns from the AED prompted protocol to advisory monitoring. Verify the actual displayed mode and local configuration; this action does not prove entry into unrestricted manual operation.
已核对的配置流程中，LEAD可从AED提示流程返回建议监护。要确认实际显示模式及当地配置；这一步并不能证明已经进入不受限制的手动操作。

00:24:26.184 --> 00:24:42.408
An ECG tone can reflect detected QRS activity without useful perfusion, and artifact or pacing signals can confuse rate displays. Continue direct patient assessment instead of equating every beep with a heartbeat that pumps blood.
ECG提示音可对应检测到QRS，却不代表有效灌注；伪差或起搏信号也可能干扰频率显示。应继续直接评估患者，不能把每声提示都等同于一次有效泵血。

00:24:42.408 --> 00:24:56.784
A pulse-oximeter tone depends on a usable optical signal. Poor perfusion, motion and other limitations can make it unreliable during arrest. SpO2 also does not measure carbon dioxide clearance.
血氧脉搏提示依赖可用光学信号。差灌注、移动等限制，可使其在骤停中不可靠，而且SpO2并不测二氧化碳清除。

00:24:56.784 --> 00:25:11.952
The reviewed LP15 offers SpO2 volume adjustment through its parameter menu. Know the actual unit, keep alerts usable and avoid teaching an unverified menu path as universal across models or software.
已核对的LP15可在血氧参数菜单中调节SpO2音量。应熟悉实际设备、保持提示可用，不能把未核实的菜单路径教成所有机型和软件通用。

00:25:11.952 --> 00:25:28.272
A metronome provides timing, not depth, recoil or indication for CPR. Its activity can also alter alarm behavior on the reviewed device. Verify the monitoring state again when the patient transitions to ROSC.
节拍器提供时序，不提供深度、回弹或CPR指征；在已核对设备中，它的运行还会改变报警行为。患者转换为ROSC后，应再次确认监护状态。

00:25:28.272 --> 00:25:41.304
A twelve-lead ECG uses ten electrodes to derive twelve views. The six chest leads are not six augmented limb leads, and a three-lead rhythm trace cannot replace a diagnostic twelve-lead.
12导联ECG用十个电极得到十二个观察方向。六个胸导联不是六个加压肢体导联，三导联心律条也不能代替诊断性12导联。

00:25:41.304 --> 00:25:56.928
Enter correct patient information and the demographic fields required by the actual system. The reviewed LP15 uses default assumptions if age or sex is omitted; machine unconfirmed text is not an independent diagnosis.
输入正确患者资料及实际系统要求的人口学字段。已核对的LP15在年龄或性别缺失时使用默认假设；机器未确认文字不是独立诊断。

00:25:56.928 --> 00:26:13.416
After ROSC, obtain a useful ECG at the clinically appropriate time and repeat if needed; the preceding lecture explains early-ECG timing differences. An early post-arrest trace can be misleading, so maintain the patient context.
ROSC后应在临床适当时取得有用ECG，必要时重复；前课已解释早期ECG时间差异。骤停后过早心电图可能误导，因此必须保留患者背景。

00:26:13.416 --> 00:26:28.320
Send to the correct receiving pathway and confirm receipt or report failure. A send icon, a printed strip and hospital acceptance are not the same event, and a normal-looking ECG does not erase concerning symptoms.
应发送至正确接收路径，确认收到或通报失败。发送图标、打印心电条和医院接收不是同一事件；看似正常ECG也不能抵消危险症状。

00:26:28.320 --> 00:26:43.416
The supplement describes importing monitor data into Siren and manually completing medication details and ECG times. Treat those as the described school workflow, not proof that every current software version behaves identically.
补充课描述把监护数据导入Siren，并手动补药物细节和ECG时间。应把它当作学校所描述流程，而不是所有现行软件版本都如此的证明。

00:26:43.416 --> 00:26:57.168
The reviewed EVENT menu records selected annotations; it does not automatically know every compressor exchange, drug dose or clinical decision. A generic event mark is not a complete medication entry.
已核对的EVENT菜单记录所选标记，但不会自动知道每次换手、药物剂量或临床决定。一个通用事件标记不是完整给药记录。

00:26:57.168 --> 00:27:14.376
Reconcile onset and CPR history, rhythm analyses, shock time and energy, ventilation/access, actual drug details, patient response, consultation and handover. Distinguish directly observed facts from reports by a bystander.
应核对起病及CPR经过、心律分析、电击时间和能量、通气与通路、真实给药细节、患者反应、咨询和交接，并区分亲自观察与旁观者报告。

00:27:14.376 --> 00:27:28.848
If an imported time is wrong or an event is uncertain, use the permitted correction process and explain the uncertainty. Do not invent exactness, silently change history or claim that documentation guarantees legal protection.
导入时间不对或事件不确定时，应依允许的更正流程并说明不确定。不能编造精确值、悄悄改历史，也不能声称记录能保证法律免责。

00:27:28.848 --> 00:27:45.336
The supplement mentions advisory monitoring during stable inter-facility transfers. Current PR33 describes a prescreened stable population with defined observations and consultation triggers; it is not blanket clearance for every monitored patient.
补充课提到稳定院际转运中的建议监护。现行PR33描述的是预先筛选、符合规定观察值及咨询条件的稳定患者，并非所有带监护患者都可按此转运。

00:27:45.336 --> 00:27:59.688
A newly resuscitated patient can remain critically unstable despite an organized rhythm and one acceptable pressure. Continue close assessment, resource planning and the applicable post-arrest destination decision.
刚复苏的患者即使出现规则心律和一次尚可血压，也可能仍非常不稳定。应继续密切评估、规划资源并按骤停后流程选择目的地。

00:27:59.688 --> 00:28:15.264
During an authorized IFT, new chest pain, reduced consciousness, hypotension or severe breathlessness changes the situation. Use the actual consultation and destination response rather than waiting for a shockable-rhythm alarm.
获授权院际转运中，新胸痛、意识下降、低血压或严重气促，会改变情境。应走实际咨询和目的地应对流程，不能等到可电击心律报警。

00:28:15.264 --> 00:28:28.224
Explain the distinction in a handover: baseline stability, what changed, what was measured, what was done and what help is now required. The mode name on the monitor does not define patient stability.
交接时应解释基线稳定状况、发生的变化、测量结果、已采取行动及现在需要什么帮助。监护仪的模式名称不定义患者是否稳定。

00:28:28.224 --> 00:28:41.136
The saved supplement also connects monitor skills to ACS and stroke. These are recognition and escalation applications, not evidence that every time-critical call belongs in the arrest pathway.
保存的补充课也把监护技能联系到ACS和卒中。这是在应用识别和升级能力，不代表所有紧急患者都应进入骤停流程。

00:28:41.136 --> 00:28:59.160
For suspected ACS, combine symptoms, perfusion and a quality ECG, prepare for deterioration and use the appropriate notification pathway. Neither absence of classic chest pain nor a nondiagnostic first ECG safely excludes ACS.
疑似ACS应结合症状、灌注和高质量ECG，准备处理恶化并进行适当通知。没有典型胸痛，或第一张ECG未能诊断，都不能安全排除ACS。

00:28:59.160 --> 00:29:14.616
For possible stroke, a focused screen, exact last-known-well history and glucose assessment support the next decision. A normal glucose does not rule out stroke, and a normal FAST screen does not exclude every stroke presentation.
疑似卒中时，重点筛查、准确最后正常时间和血糖评估有助于下一步决定。血糖正常不能排除卒中，FAST正常也不能排除所有卒中表现。

00:29:14.616 --> 00:29:29.400
Do not let equipment setup consume the time needed for urgent support, destination planning and pre-alert. The full ACS and stroke pathways require their own source-based teaching, not an improvised answer from an arrest slide.
不能让器械准备耗掉紧急支持、目的地规划和预通知所需时间。完整ACS与卒中流程各需有来源的教学，不能凭骤停课某页临时编答案。

00:29:29.400 --> 00:29:42.624
In this original drill, a fifty-four-year-old collapses at a community workshop. Bystanders started CPR and an AED is operating. Do not remove a working treatment before the replacement is ready.
本原创练习中，一位54岁患者在社区工作坊倒下，旁观者已经CPR，AED正在工作。替代设备未就绪前，不应移除有效治疗。

00:29:42.624 --> 00:29:56.976
A cable fault delays the incoming manual unit. Assign one person to solve that fault while the team maintains the current effective CPR and follows the usable AED workflow. Do not create an avoidable no-treatment interval.
接入的手动设备因线缆故障延迟。指定一人处理故障，其余团队维持现有有效CPR并遵循可用AED流程，不能制造本可避免的无治疗间隔。

00:29:56.976 --> 00:30:13.488
After a coordinated transition, apply the appropriate shock or no-shock sequence from the actual assessment. Later, communicate the CO2 rise and movement, assess circulation appropriately and announce a confirmed transition if supported.
协调转换后，应按实际评估执行适当电击或不电击顺序。之后出现CO2升高和活动时，先通报、适当评估循环，再在证据支持时宣布确认的状态转换。

00:30:13.488 --> 00:30:29.088
The recorder now reconciles bystander reports, device changes, delivered therapy and the patient response. Success in this drill means safe reasoning and coordinated action, not making the story end with ROSC every time.
记录者要核对旁观者报告、器械转换、实际治疗与患者反应。本练习的成功是安全推理及协调行动，不是每次都硬把故事写成ROSC。

00:30:29.088 --> 00:30:47.688
After the event, compare the actual timeline with patient needs: first effective CPR, first indicated shock, interruptions, airway performance, causes, consultation and handover. A monitor download informs this review but cannot reconstruct every human decision.
事件后，把真实时间线与患者需要比较：首次有效CPR、首次有指征电击、停顿、气道表现、病因、咨询和交接。监护下载可提供证据，却不能重建所有人的决定。

00:30:47.688 --> 00:31:01.680
Discuss system factors, skill gaps and communication using observed facts. Avoid judging the entire team only by survival, and do not promise that an operational learning review eliminates all accountability.
应根据观察事实讨论系统因素、技能缺口和沟通。不能只凭存活结果评价整个团队，也不能承诺操作学习复盘会取消一切责任。

00:31:01.680 --> 00:31:14.040
Choose a concrete improvement, such as preparing compatible connectors before an exchange or shortening a specific pause without losing the all-clear check. Rehearse the change and measure again.
选择具体改进，例如转换前备好相容接头，或在不丢掉安全确认的前提下缩短某次停顿。练习改变后，再次测量。

00:31:14.040 --> 00:31:28.344
Separate operational learning from personal psychological support. Offer appropriate voluntary resources without compelling a traumatic retelling or promising absolute confidentiality beyond the applicable framework.
操作学习应与个人心理支持区分。可提供适当自愿资源，但不强迫复述创伤，也不承诺超出适用框架的绝对保密。

00:31:28.344 --> 00:32:09.624
The literal respiratory pages connect appearance, history and examination. Observe effort, speech, chest expansion and retractions; compare both sides systematically for air entry and added sounds. Ask about baseline disease, inhaled medicines, smoking or other exposures, cough and the amount, colour and consistency of sputum. Compare with what is usual for this patient. Asymmetry, crackles or wheeze narrows questions but does not identify one disease automatically. Prioritize an unstable patient rather than finishing the routine respiratory count or interview.
字面指定呼吸页把外观、病史与检查连在一起：观察用力、讲话、胸廓扩张及凹陷，系统比较两侧进气和附加音。询问基线疾病、吸入药物、吸烟或其他暴露、咳嗽及痰量、颜色和性状，并与该患者平常情况比较。不对称、湿啰音或哮鸣有助缩小问题，但不能自动确定一种病。不稳定患者应先处理威胁，而不是完成常规呼吸计数或访谈。

00:32:09.624 --> 00:32:50.256
With an existing chest drain, include tube security, the actual drainage system, breathing findings and possible subcutaneous air in the focused assessment. This is not permission to clamp, disconnect or manipulate an unfamiliar drain. The chapter respiratory-rate examples depend on age, and its usual saturation above 95 percent is background teaching rather than a universal oxygen prescription. Link an abnormal observation to the applicable assessment and support pathway, then report the response. Hospital nursing diagnoses and ordered blood-gas sampling do not create a new paramedic procedure.
已有胸管时，重点评估还包括管路固定、真实引流系统、呼吸所见及可能的皮下气肿；这不允许随意夹闭、断开或操作不熟悉的引流管。本章呼吸频率示例依年龄而变，通常血氧高于95%的表述是背景教学，不是通用氧疗处方。异常观察应联系适用的评估支持流程，再报告反应。医院护理诊断及需医嘱的血气采样，不会创造新的救护操作权限。

00:32:50.256 --> 00:33:27.672
The topical checklist begins with a verified order and medication record, not a jar that happens to be nearby. Confirm identity with appropriate independent identifiers; connect the intended medicine, dose, route, time and indication to the actual patient, and document what was really done. The source repeats label comparisons at selection, preparation and before administration. Multiple signatures on a record do not make an unclear order reliable. Stop and clarify a mismatch rather than completing a ritual check and proceeding anyway.
外用药清单从核实处方与用药记录开始，不是从旁边刚好有的一罐药开始。用适当独立身份信息确认患者，把预定药物、剂量、途径、时间和适应证连到真实患者，并记录实际行动。来源要求取药、准备和给药前重复比对标签。记录上多人签名，不会让含糊医嘱自动可靠。遇到不符应停止澄清，不能仪式性核对后照做。

00:33:27.672 --> 00:34:13.176
Topical treatment still requires protection and a product-specific technique. Inspect the intended site, allergies and skin condition; use appropriate gloves and hand hygiene to protect the patient and avoid absorbing medication yourself. The checklist describes clearing previous product, preparing the skin and applying the ordered quantity without vigorous rubbing. Its suggestions about damp skin, a thin versus generous layer, warming a product in gloved hands or sterile gloves for lesions are not one instruction for every medicine, wound or formulation. Follow the actual product and aseptic wound-care plan; do not add heat or massage to a patch by analogy.
外用治疗仍需防护与具体产品技术。检查预定部位、过敏及皮肤状态，使用适当手套和手卫生，既保护患者，也避免自己吸收药物。清单描述清除旧药、准备皮肤及不用力摩擦地涂规定量。但湿皮肤、薄涂或厚涂、在戴手套手中温软药物、破损处用无菌手套等建议，不是对所有药物、伤口和剂型的统一指令。应依真实产品及无菌伤口计划，不能类推给贴剂加热或按摩。

00:34:13.176 --> 00:34:53.352
Protect the remaining product as well as the application site. Use the appropriate clean or sterile applicator without returning contaminated material to the container. Change soiled gloves and clean hands when moving to a clean task. Explain expected sensations, preserve comfort and privacy, and record site, product, dose or amount, time and patient response. A topical, transdermal, oral or injected formulation is not interchangeable merely because the medicine name is similar. Reconciliation includes what the patient already used, not just the next intended dose.
应用部位与剩余产品都要保护。使用适当清洁或无菌涂具，不把污染材料带回容器。由脏任务转到清洁任务时应换污染手套并清洁双手。说明预期感觉，维护舒适隐私，记录部位、产品、剂量或用量、时间及患者反应。外涂、透皮、口服或注射剂型，不能只因药名相近就互换。用药核对包括患者已经使用的药，不只是下一次打算给的剂量。

00:34:53.352 --> 00:35:40.896
The literal range then opens parenteral administration. Intradermal targets the dermis, subcutaneous the tissue beneath it, intramuscular muscle and intravenous an existing venous route or access device. IV delivery avoids an absorption step; an IM or SC injection still needs absorption and is not guaranteed to act instantly. The source image sketches IM at 90 degrees, SC at 45, IV at 25 and ID at 10-15. These are schematic examples, not universal settings: patient tissue, needle, device, medicine and the specifically trained technique determine the actual approach. This opening range does not teach every later injection checklist.
字面范围接着进入注射给药：皮内目标是真皮，皮下为其下方组织，肌内为肌肉，静脉则经静脉通路或装置。IV免去吸收步骤；IM或SC仍需吸收，不保证立即起效。来源示意图画IM为90度、SC为45度、IV为25度、ID为10至15度。这是图示例子，不是通用设置；真实方式取决于患者组织、针具、装置、药物及专项受训技术。此开头范围不等于已教授后续所有注射清单。

00:35:40.896 --> 00:36:21.312
Parenteral safety separates contamination, wrong-drug errors, sharps injury and discomfort. Prepare in a suitable clean area, protect sterile key parts, use equipment for its intended single-patient purpose and dispose of sharps safely. Changing a needle does not make a used syringe safe for another patient. The assigned table starts hand hygiene and gives an old pump-count/time example; use the actual hand-rub instructions, cover the hands and rub until dry instead of assuming every dispenser delivers the same amount. Gloves never replace hand hygiene before an aseptic task or after glove removal.
注射安全应分别考虑污染、给错药、锐器伤及不适。在适当清洁区域准备，保护关键无菌部分，按器械规定的单患者用途使用，并安全处理锐器。换针不会让用过的注射器变得可给另一患者使用。指定表从手卫生开始，并给出较旧的按泵次数和时间示例；应依实际手消毒剂说明、覆盖双手并揉至干燥，不能假定每个泵都出相同用量。无菌任务前或脱手套后，手套都不能代替手卫生。

00:36:21.312 --> 00:37:05.280
Original rehearsal: a deteriorating patient has a documented treatment, an open cream container with an unclear label and an IV already running. First address airway, breathing and perfusion, then establish what product and dose were actually used, inspect the line and clarify the unclear preparation before further administration. State which findings are observed, which are reported and which remain unknown. The assignment includes chapter references and the next chapter objectives; it does not require memorizing bibliography entries or inventing missing orders. Explain how the assessment, medicine checks and infusion chain protect this same patient.
原创演练：一名恶化患者有已记录治疗、标签不清的开封药膏，以及运行中的IV。先处理气道、呼吸和灌注，再核实实际使用的产品和剂量、检查管路，并在继续给药前澄清含糊制剂。说清哪些是观察、哪些是转述、哪些仍未知。指定范围含章节参考文献及下一章目标，不要求背文献条目或编造缺失医嘱。应解释评估、药物核对与输注链如何共同保护这个患者。

00:37:05.280 --> 00:37:44.256
The recovered March 2025 page-40 box says thirty minutes have elapsed, without the extra qualifications found in the June 2026 comparison. That later page distinguishes thirty without ROSC or defibrillation from forty if either occurred. Neither box is the complete current BCEHS decision pathway. Current R02 uses its own eligibility, consultation and rapid or minimum-duration branches. Keep the three sources distinct; a timer alone does not authorize stopping, and this comparison is not an instruction to wait before starting indicated care.
找回的2025年3月第40页框只写已过30分钟，没有2026年6月比较版的附加条件。后者区分无ROSC或电击时30分钟，以及曾有其中任一情况时40分钟。两个框都不是现行BCEHS完整决策路径；现行R02有自身适用条件、咨询及快速或最低时长分支。应分清三种来源；计时器本身不授权停止，也不能据此延后有指征的最初处理。

00:37:44.256 --> 00:38:27.912
The 2025 pages 42-43 ask for oversight after twenty minutes of high-quality CPR, when a treatable cause is identified, or when arrest occurs during transport. Page 45 links a possible moving-CPR decision to history, examination and consultation. Current R02 instead requires an early CliniCall for an EMR or PCP leading without ACP support after CPR, analysis and indicated defibrillation have begun; this may be several cycles. A request for guidance is different from a decision to terminate. Do not wait for a textbook twenty-minute point if the actual current pathway requires earlier contact.
2025年第42至43页列高质量CPR20分钟后、发现可治疗病因或转运中骤停时咨询；第45页把可能边转运边CPR的决定连到病史、检查与咨询。现行R02则要求无ACP支持、由EMR或PCP带领时，在已开始CPR、分析及有指征电击后尽早CliniCall，可能经过数轮。请求指导不同于决定终止；若真实现行路径要求更早联系，不能等教材20分钟点。

00:38:27.912 --> 00:39:13.920
The recovered 2025 nitrate card ties one dose to the strength of the patient prescription, with a three-to-five-minute interval and pressure strictly above 110. Its notes require oversight when there is no prescription; the chest-pain page also requires consultation before more than three doses. The June 2026 comparison specifies 0.4 milligrams sublingually. Current BCEHS likewise specifies 0.4 milligrams, with its own pressure-at-least-110 and heart-rate screen and consultation requirements. Do not turn one source into an unlabelled dose for another, or let a restarted pain episode erase prior intake or contraindications.
找回的2025年硝酸甘油卡把一剂联系患者处方强度，间隔3至5分钟，血压须严格高于110；注释要求无处方时咨询，胸痛页还要求超过三剂前咨询。2026年6月比较版明确0.4 mg舌下；现行BCEHS也明确0.4 mg，并有自身血压至少110、心率筛查和咨询要求。不能把一来源剂量无标示地套到另一来源，也不能让复发的一轮疼痛抹去既往摄入或禁忌。

00:39:13.920 --> 00:40:00.984
Original source-selection exercise: a patient remains in arrest at thirty minutes, and a teammate points to the recovered single-line box. Explain what is missing before any discontinuation decision: the actual applicable pathway, rhythm and ROSC history, treatable causes, clinical circumstances and consultation or standing direction. Then repeat the exercise for nitrate treatment when the prescription strength or previous doses are unclear. In both cases, clarify the real source and patient information instead of choosing the most permissive sentence. The 2025 page also lacks the later pediatric-pad sentence; pediatric AED and LP15 restrictions remain a separately labelled comparison.
原创来源选择练习：患者30分钟时仍骤停，队友指着找回副本的一行框。说明任何终止决定前还缺什么：实际适用路径、心律和ROSC经过、可治疗病因、临床情境，以及咨询或既有指示。再用处方强度或已给剂量不明的硝酸甘油治疗重复练习。两者都应澄清真实来源及患者信息，不能选最宽松一句。2025页还没有后来的儿童电极句，儿童AED与LP15限制仍作为另行标示的比较。

00:40:00.984 --> 00:40:12.888
Close the lesson by talking through one full rhythm assessment from ongoing CPR to the next intervention. Name who performs each action and what evidence supports the decision.
结束前，从持续CPR开始，把一次完整心律评估讲到下一项干预，并说明每项行动由谁做、决定依据是什么。

00:40:12.888 --> 00:40:22.392
Then change the rhythm to nonshockable after charging. Explain disarming and prompt CPR rather than delivering a shock just because the device is ready.
再把情境改为充能后发现不可电击心律。应解释撤能及迅速恢复CPR，而不是因为器械准备好了就电击。

00:40:22.392 --> 00:40:33.168
Next remove the advisory alarm while the patient becomes pulseless. Explain why no alarm does not prove circulation and how direct assessment changes the plan.
接着取消建议报警，同时患者变成无脉搏。解释为何没有报警不证明有循环，以及直接评估如何改变计划。

00:40:33.168 --> 00:40:46.632
Finally distinguish school examples, manufacturer instructions, operational authority and current clinical pathways. That separation is part of competence, not an optional footnote after memorizing the technique.
最后，区分学校示例、厂家说明、操作权限及现行临床流程。能够区分这些本身就是能力的一部分，不是背完技术后可有可无的脚注。
